  "rationale": "Only non-perfect judge is summary_quality=0.934 (headroom ~0.033) and the parent eval still exposes no per-example telemetry, so a content-level mutation is a shot in the dark. Round 1's edit_skill on section_summary.md (coverage + no-paraphrase + normative-obligation nudges) proved that any directional content push on this scaffold inflates output length and regresses all three judges by ~0.11 \u2014 one example truncated to 0/0/0. Round 2 therefore noop'd, declaring sampling 'exhausted' at T=0.1; that's an over-statement. The task is deterministic structured JSON extraction \u2014 greedy decoding (T=0.0) is the canonical setting, strictly more deterministic than 0.1, and it (a) adds no new instruction surface so cannot clash with hierarchy/section_summary/citations/exclusions/output_schema the way the Round-6-class skill addition did (\u22120.194 in the legacy run), and (b) does not increase average output length, so it cannot reproduce the Round-1 truncation failure. Expected effect: picks the mode of the token distribution on quoted phrases and legal-term verbatim preservation, which maps to the faithfulness and accuracy sub-criteria of summary_quality. Predicted \u0394: +0.000 to +0.015 on summary_quality (aggregate ~0.967 \u2192 0.967\u20130.98); worst case is a true no-op if the Databricks endpoint already treats near-zero temperatures identically, in which case we've still cleanly eliminated one lever at zero risk.",
